.SH "Enumeration Type Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "enum \fBSystemEx\&.AI\&.BackendCapabilities\fP : int"

.PP
Defines capability flags for \fBAI\fP backends\&. Naming follows the AI_BACKEND_CAPS_XXX convention\&. These flags describe what features a backend supports, such as text generation, audio processing, vision models, tool execution, platform integration, and hardware acceleration\&.

.PP
Describes capabilities supported by an \fBAI\fP backend\&.

.PP
This enum is intentionally broad and future-proof\&. It covers:
.IP "\(bu" 2
Local and remote execution
.IP "\(bu" 2
GPU/CPU/WASM/native runtimes
.IP "\(bu" 2
Text, chat, audio, vision, video, multimodal
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBTools\fP, agents, function calling
.IP "\(bu" 2
Embeddings, vector search, batch processing
.IP "\(bu" 2
Platform-specific capabilities (Windows, Web, Mobile)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Custom developer-defined capabilities
.PP

.PP
Naming follows AI_BACKEND_CAPS_XXX\&. 
.PP
